.TH "ZYPPER-DECLARATIVE" "1" "May 2026" "zypper-declarative 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
zypper-declarative - declarative, reconciling converger surfaced as a
zypper subcommand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]zypper declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R] [\f[I]key=value\f[R] \&...]
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R] [\f[I]key=value\f[R] \&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] converges a SUSE system to a desired
manifest expressed in the declarable subset of the SUSE Machinery
system-description format: the \f[I]packages\f[R],
\f[I]repositories\f[R], \f[I]services\f[R], and \f[I]config_files\f[R]
scopes.
The canonical serialisation is JSON (Machinery format_version 1); YAML
is an opt-in serialisation of the identical data model.
.PP
Convergence happens inside a single snapshot transaction.
What was applied is recorded as an \f[I]applied record\f[R] under
\f[V]/usr/lib/zypper-declarative/applied.json\f[R] within the
generation, so a rollback restores the matching declaration.
The tool is idempotent: a second run against an unchanged manifest and
an undrifted system makes no changes.
.SH VERBS
.TP
\f[B]apply\f[R]
Converge the system to the desired manifest inside a snapshot
transaction.
.TP
\f[B]diff\f[R]
Dry run.
Print what \f[B]apply\f[R] would change.
Makes no modification.
.TP
\f[B]verify\f[R]
Check whether the actual state equals the applied record, modulo the
keep-list.
Reads live state, or a supplied state dump (\f[B]state-path=\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R]
Print the current declarative state: applied manifest hash, generation,
resolved package count, and a one-line drift summary.
.TP
\f[B]describe\f[R]
Read the actual state of the declarable scopes and emit it as a manifest
(canonical JSON by default, YAML on request).
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
Options use \f[B]key=value\f[R] syntax and precede any bare-word
argument.
Control via environment variables is not supported.
.TP
\f[B]mode=auto|external|internal\f[R]
Transaction binding.
Default \f[I]auto\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]manifest-path=\f[R]<path>
Desired manifest path.
Default from configuration.
.TP
\f[B]format=json|yaml\f[R]
Manifest input format (for \f[B]apply\f[R]/\f[B]diff\f[R]) and
\f[B]describe\f[R] output format.
Default \f[I]json\f[R], otherwise inferred from the file extension.
.TP
\f[B]state-path=\f[R]<path>
A state dump in the shared schema, used as the actual-state source for
\f[B]verify\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]root=\f[R]<path>
Root to describe (and the actual-state root for read-only verbs).
Default \f[V]/\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]out=\f[R]<path>
\f[B]describe\f[R] output file.
Default standard output.
.TP
\f[B]applied-root=\f[R]<path>
Generation root from which the applied record is read.
Default \f[V]/\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]keep-list=\f[R]<path>
Allowlist of persistent-but-undeclared paths never reported or deleted.
.TP
\f[B]content-store=\f[R]<path>
Base path for resolving config_files \f[I]content_ref\f[R] values at
apply time.
.TP
\f[B]repo-lock=\f[R]<repo>
Fallback pinned repository used only when the manifest declares no
\f[I]repositories\f[R] scope.
.TP
\f[B]signature-verification=on|off\f[R], \f[B]keyring=\f[R]<path>
Enable or disable manifest signature verification.
Default \f[I]on\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]activation-policy=reboot|soft-reboot|none\f[R]
How \f[B]apply\f[R] schedules activation of a freshly sealed snapshot.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]version\f[R]
Print the version and embedded spec hash, then exit 0.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
Print usage, then exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Success: convergence complete or a no-op, system matches the
declaration, or \f[B]describe\f[R] produced output.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Logical failure: convergence failed and was discarded; \f[B]verify\f[R]
found drift; manifest invalid, unsafe-YAML, or unverified; state
collection failed.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Invocation error: bad arguments; unknown format value; manifest
unreadable; insufficient privilege; transaction mechanism unavailable;
output path unwritable; malformed state dump.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[V]/usr/lib/zypper-declarative/applied.json\f[R]
The applied record of a generation.
.TP
\f[V]/etc/etc.syncpoint\f[R]
Never written to or deleted.
.SH INSTALLATION
.PP
Install from the openSUSE Build Service:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
zypper install zypper-declarative
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
On Debian/Ubuntu derivatives:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
apt install zypper-declarative
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
On Fedora-family systems:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dnf install zypper-declarative
\f[R]
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\f[B]zypper\f[R](8), \f[B]snapper\f[R](8),
\f[B]transactional-update\f[R](8), \f[B]systemctl\f[R](1)
